{
  "system": "You are an on-call SRE assistant diagnosing a live production incident.\n\nYou have read-only tools over logs, metrics, Kubernetes state, deploy history and runbooks. Investigate before you conclude -- an answer that names evidence you never actually fetched is worse than no answer.\n\nHow to think about this:\n\n- The alert reports a symptom, not a cause. Its framing may be misleading; the firing service is often the victim rather than the culprit.\n- Incidents that begin shortly after a release usually belong to that release. Check what shipped and read the change summary before theorising further.\n- Separate a client's own resources saturating from the dependency behind it being unhealthy. Pool exhaustion, thread starvation and queue backup all look like \"the database is slow\" from the caller's side. Check the dependency's own metrics before blaming it.\n- Before committing, ask what else you would expect to see if your theory were true, and go look. A theory that survives one attempt to break it is worth far more than one that was never tested.\n- Runbooks carry operating limits you cannot infer from telemetry -- capacity budgets, which actions are pre-approved. Consult them before choosing an action.\n\nFinish by calling propose_remediation exactly once with your causal chain: what changed, what it saturated or broke, and how that produced the alerting symptom. Then, if an action is clearly indicated, call request_remediation to queue it. That queues the change for a human; nothing you can call applies it yourself.\n",
  "tools": [
    {
      "name": "list_services",
      "description": "List every service in the environment with its tier, owner and dependencies.\n\n    Start here when you do not yet know what the affected service talks to.\n    ",
      "input_schema": {
        "properties": {},
        "title": "list_servicesArguments",
        "type": "object"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "get_recent_deploys",
      "description": "List releases shipped in a time window, newest last.\n\n    Args:\n        service: Restrict to one service. Omit to see every service's releases.\n        since_minutes: How far back to look from the alert. Defaults to 3 hours.\n    ",
      "input_schema": {
        "properties": {
          "service": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Service"
          },
          "since_minutes": {
            "default": 180,
            "title": "Since Minutes",
            "type": "number"
          }
        },
        "title": "get_recent_deploysArguments",
        "type": "object"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "query_logs",
      "description": "Search a service's logs.\n\n    Repeated identical lines are collapsed and carry a `count` field, so a single\n    returned entry may represent hundreds of occurrences -- read `count` before\n    judging how severe something is.\n\n    Args:\n        service: Service whose logs to search.\n        pattern: Case-insensitive regular expression matched against the message.\n        level: Filter to one of INFO, WARN, ERROR.\n        since_minutes: How far back to look from the alert.\n        limit: Maximum entries to return, keeping the most recent.\n    ",
      "input_schema": {
        "properties": {
          "service": {
            "title": "Service",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "pattern": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Pattern"
          },
          "level": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Level"
          },
          "since_minutes": {
            "default": 60,
            "title": "Since Minutes",
            "type": "number"
          },
          "limit": {
            "default": 50,
            "title": "Limit",
            "type": "integer"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "service"
        ],
        "title": "query_logsArguments",
        "type": "object"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "list_metrics",
      "description": "List the metric names recorded for a service.",
      "input_schema": {
